art+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e38feeccfd89541c2094cf839159dba70f6297504ba27e2351563a105e4b6b0a","event_uuid":"c64fd53d-db9d-46b6-8c27-fa6cfe994809","position":{"commit_sha":"ccf03249aaaea3776a661a3a67f98fcad5498f06","position":"1788564338720295544-c64fd53d-db9d-46b6-8c27-fa6cfe994809"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"07b2ec76a773202115bacac5a55fc46b79fc1105d17a3be3b030a3e9fcf90e3f","event_uuid":"839bb8de-0a42-43b1-aa2c-3e49bb8b73f1","position":{"commit_sha":"035f320030ba42c679ee9824ebf640f7233f97fc","position":"1788564358983932359-839bb8de-0a42-43b1-aa2c-3e49bb8b73f1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Production-source audit complete at `9e65567b79ff`: 1,012 tracked paths accounted for in 32 shards (≤30 files each); 922 authored files audited, 90 generated/vendored/data paths excluded, and 275 files reported as remediation candidates. Exclusions: generated CLI help/assets/manifests, marked generated types, lock/baseline/result data, wordlists, and a pinned vendored rule bundle. Candidate ranges and behavior-bearing docstring consumers were captured for validation before child creation. Unit-test audit is in progress.","timestamp":1788554094173617402},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Tracker fallback note: rebar MCP became unavailable with repeated HTTP 502 responses during child reconciliation. The recurrence was added to existing bug witted-invisible-roan and linked to this epic. Local CLI fallback repaired the missing file-impact records on culm-private-beetle and cipolin-undyed-kangaroo.","timestamp":1788555640273334001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Audit inventory complete at `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n- Production: 1,012 tracked; 922 audited; 90 excluded; 275 affected.\n- Tests: 1,959 tracked; 1,849 audited; 110 excluded; 1,073 affected.\n- Scripts: 101 tracked; 99 audited; 2 excluded; 56 affected.\n- Infrastructure/GitHub: 164 tracked; 154 audited; 10 excluded; 95 affected.\n- Total: 3,236 tracked; 3,024 audited; 212 excluded; 1,499 affected.\n\nCreated 1,499 direct child tickets, one per affected file. Validation found 1,499 unique target paths; every child has exactly one file-impact path matching its title, with zero missing, mismatched, or duplicate paths. Consumer paths remain in child descriptions as preservation context, not edit impacts. The later MCP timeout is tracked by linked bug `skaldic-carbon-copperhead`. The epic remains in progress until all remediation children are implemented and closed.","timestamp":1788564358983932359}],"created_at":1788550666739458658,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"29e0f405-b7da-457d-8d8a-9806a1344b04","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"95c1-f6eb-0fa9-402e"},{"link_uuid":"45e357da-be99-4419-b513-71066d84a16e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9ea3-7d07-ea55-4496"}],"description":"## Context\nAudit authored code and configuration for comments or docstrings that add repetition, obvious narration, duplicated documentation, or excessive history. Preserve non-obvious invariants, safety constraints, compatibility contracts, citations, surprising behavior, and user-facing text.\n\n## Scope\nInclude authored text files under `src/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`, `infra/`, and `.github/`. Exclude generated or vendored files, binaries, lockfiles, snapshots or fixtures used only as test data, and symlinks. Record every excluded path or category with the shard manifest. Treat docstrings consumed by CLI help, documentation generation, cross-module `.__doc__` access, or content-asserting tests as behavior-bearing contract surfaces.\n\n## Plan\n- Partition the included paths into small read-only audit shards.\n- Validate findings and create one child task per affected file.\n- Each child names the locations, concise replacement or authoritative target, preserve list, and any external docstring consumers.\n- Record consumer paths in each child's description; include only expected edit targets in file impact, then independently land each remediation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every included file appears in exactly one recorded audit shard.\n- [ ] Every excluded path or category is recorded with the shard manifest.\n- [ ] Every confirmed affected file has exactly one child task with precise file impact.\n- [ ] Each child records the rationale, contracts, citations, and user-facing text to preserve.\n- [ ] Each remediated diff retains or relocates every preserve-list item.\n- [ ] Each child identifies docstring consumers or records that none were found.\n- [ ] All child tasks are closed after their stated acceptance criteria are met.\n- [ ] The epic records the final shard manifest and child-ticket inventory.\n\n## Verification\n- Diff the recorded included and excluded paths against `rtk git ls-files src scripts tests infra .github`; every tracked path must be accounted for once.\n- Search for `__doc__` consumers and content assertions before changing each flagged docstring; run the affected help and tests.\n- For Python files under `src/`, `tests/`, or `scripts/`, run `rtk .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`; exit 0 proves only that no uncited history token remains.\n- For every child, manually review its diff against the recorded preserve list. This is the authoritative check for bloat and for all files outside the guard's Python-only scan.\n- Inspect epic children and file-impact records through rebar MCP; each confirmed target path must appear once.\n- Before closing the epic, confirm every child is closed.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","95c1-f6eb-0fa9-402e"],["relates_to","9ea3-7d07-ea55-4496"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Coordination and audit only; repository edits belong to child tasks with per-file impact.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"3e6ea7ab-628b-4640-ae5c-b09dd6146f1d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["documentation","maintainability","comments"],"ticket_id":"d8a3-ff71-8112-4e55","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Remediate bloated source comments","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["327bf8d1-8e03-44b4-a546-68d6e810bac8","6b040748-df8e-4992-b8d2-9aed52c3a8f3","29e0f405-b7da-457d-8d8a-9806a1344b04","fb6400d5-1dd7-4f40-b886-cfe51a0e4ef5","d8ddee8b-9fac-4eba-b77a-a9e74a23fef0","2ca79464-d273-4f24-9ec4-16d6a1701b52","17f785b2-27c0-494b-8037-b35e1d7b4aff","0f354e14-ea66-4808-8dd4-ecd86b12ea17","3e6ea7ab-628b-4640-ae5c-b09dd6146f1d","2b155c82-3f31-49a2-a325-bab4a6240bae","f0ea24e0-faea-4196-bf07-1bf27ee34966","45e357da-be99-4419-b513-71066d84a16e","ee992169-56a8-44b5-b566-5ad159e95cde","c64fd53d-db9d-46b6-8c27-fa6cfe994809","839bb8de-0a42-43b1-aa2c-3e49bb8b73f1"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788568417987110320,"uuid":"dbb22012-9d2d-4bce-b3aa-21aea0ad5434"}